  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Edge and identity",
      "items": [
        "Traefik (skfence, or skfenceha for the HA multi-manager alternative) terminates TLS.",
        "sksec's CrowdSec bouncer sits in front as a forwardAuth middleware, fail-closed.",
        "sksso (Authentik) is the forward-auth default for skpulse, skpatch, and skhome, and the OIDC app for skmesh."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ops and patching",
      "items": [
        "skgit is the repo of record; skflow (Windmill) is where the skpatch program's Renovate and SBOM flows will live.",
        "skbom (Dependency-Track + Trivy) and the skflow f/skpatch, f/skrelease, f/ops flows are planned, not yet running, per docs/skpatch-program.md.",
        "skpatch itself, the host-patching role and dashboard, is live today.",
        "skmon (Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Jaeger) scrapes metrics across the whole fleet; skport is the Swarm web UI."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Data",
      "items": [
        "Postgres 17 (skmem-pg), FalkorDB (skgraph), Qdrant (skvector), Syncthing (sksync), Garage S3 (skstor).",
        "skreg (Docker Registry v2) is the one tracked exception left floating, unpinned by design today.",
        "skbackup takes snapshots and ships them offsite via restic, consuming skstor as its offsite target."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Apps and comms",
      "items": [
        "15 optional self-hosted apps (skhub, skgallery, skpulse, skmail, and more) ride the same Traefik edge; every one of them is listed in data/status.json's pinned-image table.",
        "SKChat and SKComms are SKWorld comms products; they are not yet rows in the v1 service catalog."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
